{
	"info": {
		"name": "Codeware API",
		"description": "Codeware REST API (v1) — public storefront endpoints, customer account (auth + profile), and admin CRUD.\n\n---\n\n**Setup**\n\n1. Set `base_url` — defaults to the local Herd/Laragon host, `https://codeware.test/api/v1`. The `/api/v1` prefix is part of the value.\n2. Run `Auth > Register` or `Auth > Login` once. The test script captures `data.token` into the `customer_token` collection variable automatically, so every authenticated customer request works from then on.\n3. For the **Admin** folder, log in with an *admin* account through `Auth > Login`, then copy the returned `data.token` into the `admin_token` collection variable. There is no separate admin login endpoint — admin vs customer is just a role on the same `users` table, and the same `Auth > Login` request serves both.\n4. Public endpoints need no auth at all.\n\n---\n\n**Conventions**\n\n**Response envelope.** There is no `JsonResource` — each controller hand-builds the body.\n\n- Paginated: `{ \"data\": [...], \"meta\": { \"current_page\", \"last_page\", \"per_page\", \"total\" } }`. `meta` has exactly those four keys, always. `GET /products` adds `meta.attributes` (facet list); `GET /notifications` adds `meta.unread_count`.\n- Single resource, create, update: `{ \"data\": { ... } }` — **no `meta` key at all**.\n- Un-paginated lists (`/pages`, `/product-categories`, `/settings/public`, `/layout`, `/cms`, and admin `/admin/pages`, `/admin/product-categories`, `/admin/settings`): `{ \"data\": [...] }`, no `meta`, and `?per_page` is ignored.\n- Deletes return `204` with an empty body.\n\n**Errors.** Laravel's stock shapes — the key is always `message`, never `error`. No global JSON exception renderer exists, so:\n\n- `422` validation → `{ \"message\": \"The given data was invalid.\", \"errors\": { \"field\": [\"...\"] } }`\n- `401` → `{ \"message\": \"Unauthenticated.\" }`\n- `403` → `{ \"message\": \"This action is unauthorized.\" }` (also returned for a blocked account or a deactivated role — the middleware revokes the token)\n- `404` → `{ \"message\": \"Not Found\" }`\n- `429` → `{ \"message\": \"Too Many Attempts.\" }`, `503` → shop closed for new orders\n\n> The collection sets `Accept: application/json` on every request. Without it Laravel does not treat the call as a JSON call, so a 422 comes back as a **302 redirect** and a 401 as a **redirect to the web login page** instead of a JSON error body.\n\n**`?locale=`.** Accepts the `code` of any active row in the `languages` table (`en` and `bn` as seeded). An unrecognised value is silently ignored rather than rejected. Honoured by `/posts`, `/pages`, `/products`, `/product-categories`, `/services`, `/settings/public` and `/vouchers` only — **no admin endpoint reads it**, so admin responses always return every translation as a `{ en: ..., bn: ... }` map.\n\n**`?per_page=`.** Defaults to the `pagination_per_page` setting (10) on public endpoints and to 15 (30 for media) on admin ones. Capped at 100, except comments and reviews which cap at 50.\n\n**Translatable fields.** Writes are nested — `\"title\": { \"en\": \"...\", \"bn\": \"...\" }` — while admin *reads* come back as the whole map. Asymmetric by design; both spellings are shown in the request bodies below.\n\n---\n\n**Not in this collection.** Themes and plugins have no REST surface at all — they are filesystem modules under `themes/{slug}/` and `plugins/{slug}/`, managed through Admin → Theme Settings and Admin → Plugin Settings. The storefront itself (shop, cart, checkout, account pages) is rendered server-side by Blade, not served over `/api/v1`.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "codeware"
	},
	"header": [
		{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
	],
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "base_url", "value": "https://codeware.test/api/v1", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "locale", "value": "en", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "per_page", "value": "15", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "customer_token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "admin_token", "value": "", "type": "string", "description": "Sanctum personal access token for the Admin folder. Run Auth > Login with an admin account and paste the data.token from the response. Set it here rather than in the environment: a collection variable shadows one of the same name in the environment, so a token pasted into the environment is silently ignored while this stays empty." },
		{ "key": "product_slug", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "product_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "category_slug", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "category_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "post_slug", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "post_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "page_slug", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "page_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "media_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "contact_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "order_number", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "order_email", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "reset_token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "user_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "chat_token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "subscriber_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "device_id", "value": "test-device-1", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "notification_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "service_slug", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "voucher_slug", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "voucher_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "comment_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "review_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "social_provider", "value": "google", "type": "string" }
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Auth",
			"description": "Customer account auth — API-only, backed by the same `users` table as the admin/Fortify web login.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Register",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
									"    const body = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.collectionVariables.set('customer_token', body.data.token);",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"name\": \"Jane Customer\",\n    \"email\": \"jane@example.com\",\n    \"password\": \"password\",\n    \"password_confirmation\": \"password\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": "{{base_url}}/auth/register"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Login",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
									"    const body = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.collectionVariables.set('customer_token', body.data.token);",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"email\": \"jane@example.com\",\n    \"password\": \"password\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": "{{base_url}}/auth/login"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Logout",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{customer_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
						"url": "{{base_url}}/auth/logout"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Forgot Password",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// The reset link is emailed (or logged, if MAIL_MAILER=log locally) — copy the",
									"// `token` query param from it into the `reset_token` collection variable."
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"email\": \"jane@example.com\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": "{{base_url}}/auth/forgot-password"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Reset Password",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"token\": \"{{reset_token}}\",\n    \"email\": \"jane@example.com\",\n    \"password\": \"new-password\",\n    \"password_confirmation\": \"new-password\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": "{{base_url}}/auth/reset-password"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Verify Email (signed link)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"description": "This exact URL (with real `id`/`hash`/`expires`/`signature`) is what's emailed on registration — paste it in from the email rather than editing the placeholders here, since the signature is cryptographically tied to those values.",
						"url": "{{base_url}}/auth/email/verify/1/REPLACE_WITH_HASH_FROM_EMAIL?expires=9999999999&signature=REPLACE_WITH_SIGNATURE_FROM_EMAIL"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Resend Verification Email",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{customer_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
						"url": "{{base_url}}/auth/email/resend"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Social Login Redirect",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"description": "Returns the OAuth provider's consent URL in `data.url` (Google or Facebook — switches on `{{social_provider}}`).",
						"url": "{{base_url}}/auth/{{social_provider}}/redirect"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Social Login Callback",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"description": "The provider redirects back here after the user approves; this 302s the browser to `{FRONTEND_URL}/auth/callback` with `?token=` (on success) or `?error=`. In Postman just check the Location header — it isn't a JSON response.",
						"url": "{{base_url}}/auth/{{social_provider}}/callback"
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Profile",
			"description": "The authenticated customer's own account.",
			"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{customer_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get Profile",
					"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/profile" }
				},
				{
					"name": "Update Profile",
					"request": {
						"method": "PUT",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"name\": \"Jane Updated\",\n    \"email\": \"jane@example.com\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": "{{base_url}}/profile"
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Firebase",
			"description": "FCM device token registration — App\\Support\\Firebase::sendToUser() pushes to every token a user has registered here.",
			"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{customer_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Register Device Token",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"token\": \"REPLACE_WITH_FCM_DEVICE_TOKEN\",\n    \"device_id\": \"{{device_id}}\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": "{{base_url}}/firebase/tokens"
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Remove Device Token",
					"request": { "method": "DELETE", "url": "{{base_url}}/firebase/tokens/{{device_id}}" }
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Notifications",
			"description": "The authenticated user's own database notifications — API equivalent of the admin bell (Livewire\\Admin\\Notifications\\Bell).",
			"auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{customer_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "List Notifications",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/notifications?per_page={{per_page}}&status=",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["notifications"],
							"query": [
								{ "key": "per_page", "value": "{{per_page}}" },
								{ "key": "status", "value": "unread", "disabled": true }
							]
						}
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Mark Notification As Read",
					"request": { "method": "POST", "url": "{{base_url}}/notifications/{{notification_id}}/read" }
				},
				{
					"name": "Mark All Notifications As Read",
					"request": { "method": "POST", "url": "{{base_url}}/notifications/read-all" }
				},
				{
					"name": "Delete Notification",
					"request": { "method": "DELETE", "url": "{{base_url}}/notifications/{{notification_id}}" }
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Public",
			"description": "No authentication required. Errors still come back as JSON — see the collection description for the envelope, the `?locale=` / `?per_page` rules and why `Accept: application/json` is set collection-wide.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Products",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "List Products",
							"request": {
								"method": "GET",
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{base_url}}/products?locale={{locale}}&per_page={{per_page}}&category={{category_slug}}&search=&featured=",
									"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
									"path": ["products"],
									"query": [
										{ "key": "locale", "value": "{{locale}}" },
										{ "key": "per_page", "value": "{{per_page}}" },
										{ "key": "category", "value": "{{category_slug}}" },
										{ "key": "search", "value": "", "disabled": true },
										{ "key": "featured", "value": "1", "disabled": true }
									]
								}
							}
						},
						{
							"name": "Get Product by Slug",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/products/{{product_slug}}?locale={{locale}}" }
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Product Categories",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "List Product Categories",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/product-categories?locale={{locale}}" }
						},
						{
							"name": "Get Product Category by Slug",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/product-categories/{{category_slug}}?locale={{locale}}" }
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Services",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "List Services",
							"request": {
								"method": "GET",
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{base_url}}/services?locale={{locale}}&per_page={{per_page}}&search=",
									"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
									"path": ["services"],
									"query": [
										{ "key": "locale", "value": "{{locale}}" },
										{ "key": "per_page", "value": "{{per_page}}" },
										{ "key": "search", "value": "", "disabled": true }
									]
								}
							}
						},
						{
							"name": "Get Service by Slug",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/services/{{service_slug}}?locale={{locale}}" }
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Posts",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "List Posts",
							"request": {
								"method": "GET",
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{base_url}}/posts?locale={{locale}}&per_page={{per_page}}&category={{category_slug}}&search=",
									"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
									"path": ["posts"],
									"query": [
										{ "key": "locale", "value": "{{locale}}" },
										{ "key": "per_page", "value": "{{per_page}}" },
										{ "key": "category", "value": "{{category_slug}}" },
										{ "key": "search", "value": "", "disabled": true }
									]
								}
							}
						},
						{
							"name": "Get Post by Slug",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/posts/{{post_slug}}?locale={{locale}}" }
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Pages",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "List Pages",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/pages?locale={{locale}}" }
						},
						{
							"name": "Get Page by Slug",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/pages/{{page_slug}}?locale={{locale}}" }
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Settings",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "Get Public Settings",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/settings/public" }
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Layout",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "Get Layout",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/layout" }
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "CMS",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "Get CMS Sections for Page",
							"request": {
								"method": "GET",
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{base_url}}/cms?page=home&name=",
									"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
									"path": ["cms"],
									"query": [
										{ "key": "page", "value": "home" },
										{ "key": "name", "value": "hero", "disabled": true }
									]
								}
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Contacts",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "Submit Contact Form",
							"request": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n    \"full_name\": \"John Doe\",\n    \"phone_number\": \"+8801700000000\",\n    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",\n    \"subject\": \"General inquiry\",\n    \"message\": \"I'd like to know more about your products.\"\n}",
									"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
								},
								"url": "{{base_url}}/contacts"
							}
						},
						{
							"name": "Request Demo",
							"request": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n    \"full_name\": \"John Doe\",\n    \"phone_number\": \"+8801700000000\",\n    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",\n    \"company\": \"Acme Corp\",\n    \"message\": \"I'd like a demo of your platform.\"\n}",
									"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
								},
								"url": "{{base_url}}/request-demo"
							}
						},
						{
							"name": "Book Demo",
							"request": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n    \"full_name\": \"John Doe\",\n    \"phone_number\": \"+8801700000000\",\n    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",\n    \"company\": \"Acme Corp\",\n    \"preferred_date\": \"2026-10-01\",\n    \"preferred_time\": \"3:00 PM\",\n    \"message\": \"Looking forward to seeing a live walkthrough.\"\n}",
									"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
								},
								"url": "{{base_url}}/book-demo"
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Subscribers",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "Subscribe",
							"request": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n    \"email\": \"subscriber@example.com\"\n}",
									"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
								},
								"url": "{{base_url}}/subscribers"
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Cart",
					"description": "Session-backed shopping cart — rides a cookie from the session middleware (no auth). Prices are recomputed server-side, so the API never trusts client amounts. Ordering is handled by the Orders endpoints.",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "Get Cart",
							"request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/cart" }
						},
						{
							"name": "Add to Cart",
							"request": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n    \"product_id\": {{product_id}},\n    \"quantity\": 1,\n    \"attributes\": { \"size\": \"42\" }\n}",
									"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
								},
								"url": "{{base_url}}/cart"
							}
						},
						{
							"name": "Update Cart Item",
							"request": {
								"method": "PUT",
								"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n    \"quantity\": 2,\n    \"attributes\": { \"size\": \"42\" }\n}",
									"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
								},
								"url": "{{base_url}}/cart/items/{{product_id}}"
							}
						},
						{
							"name": "Remove Cart Item",
							"request": { "method": "DELETE", "url": "{{base_url}}/cart/items/{{product_id}}" }
						},
						{
							"name": "Clear Cart",
							"request": { "method": "DELETE", "url": "{{base_url}}/cart" }
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Comments",
					"description": "Comments on Posts, Products, and Services. Listing is public; posting a comment/reply or deleting your own requires a logged-in customer account.",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "List Comments",
							"request": {
								"method": "GET",
								"url": {
